    <string name="about_tagline">Videos, songs, karaoke and two-language subtitles in over 300 languages, made for the TV remote.</string>
    <string name="about_text">Free and open source. No ads, no account, no tracking: the app collects no data about you. Videos, songs and texts stream from the public media library of jw.org, and nothing is stored on the TV unless you download it.</string>
    <string name="about_made_by">Made by Maksym Chapliak in Montreal</string>
    <string name="about_legal">Cedar TV is an independent, unofficial app. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by jw.org or any organization. All content belongs to its owners.</string>
    <string name="tour_t1">Welcome to Cedar TV</string>
    <string name="tour_b1">Watch videos, listen to songs and sing along, in over 300 languages.\n\nA quick tour: 5 short pages.</string>
    <string name="tour_t2">Your remote</string>
    <string name="tour_b2">Arrows   move around\nOK   select\nHold OK   menu with favorite and download\nBack   go back or close\nHome   leave the app</string>
    <string name="tour_t3">The home screen</string>
    <string name="tour_b3">Watch TV: random videos, no music\nLibrary · Music &amp; Audio · Karaoke\nTop right: Search, Subtitles (CC), Language, Settings</string>
    <string name="tour_t4">While watching</string>
    <string name="tour_b4">Press Up (or the CC button in the controls) for subtitles, quality, favorite and download.\n\nSubtitles in a second language are a great way to learn: choose CC at the top of the home screen.\n\nLeft and Right skip 10 seconds.</string>
    <string name="tour_t5">Good to know</string>
    <string name="tour_b5">Downloads play without internet.\nAfter a few minutes of rest, a screensaver shows artwork, the clock and today\'s daily text.\nChange these in Settings (the gear), where you can also replay this tour.</string>
